Right now we have:
    static c10::optional<DispatchKey> dispatchKeySetToDispatchKey_(const DispatchKeySet& keySet) {
      if (C10_UNLIKELY(keySet.empty())) {
        return c10::nullopt;
      }

      return impl::dispatchTypeId(keySet);
    }


The empty key set test is unnecessary as dispatchTypeId is total and will return an UndefinedDispatchKey when the key set is empty.
This is a pretty easy fix and would be a good bootcamp/starter task for someone looking to work on the dispatcher.
